findings.evidence:
With the task's own oracle, these graphs all pass V6:
- alt3/P1_noise_removed.grc: the noise source and its path deleted, adder reduced to 3 inputs;
- alt3/P2_noise_008.grc: noise amplitude 0.08 (4x);
- alt3/P3_noise_uniform.grc: uniform noise instead of Gaussian.

The noise is measurable. Noise alone gives a ch2 rms of about 0.011 (reference value 0.011245), so a floor catches its removal. With a ch2 min of 0.005 added (task_n512_floor.json), P1 fails V6 while the reference, v1-v3 and all correct alternatives still pass.

P4_samprate_32k.grc (samp_rate reverted to 32000) also passes. That one is inherently unobservable because every tone is defined as a fraction of samp_rate, and the author's notes already say so. It needs no fix.
